Two NVIDIA Cosmos projects are wrapped as NPA workbench tools and invoked by the
`physical-ai-data-factory` blueprint. Both are Apache-2.0.

## Cosmos Evaluator

  https://github.com/nvidia-cosmos/cosmos-evaluator            (Apache-2.0)

Wrapped by `npa/src/npa/workbench/cosmos_evaluator/` and exposed as
`npa workbench cosmos-evaluator`. Two of upstream's checks are used:

  - Hallucination check (`checks/hallucination`). NPA runs upstream's own
    `HallucinationProcessor` when an upstream checkout is importable
    (`NPA_COSMOS_EVALUATOR_SRC`, else `/opt/cosmos-evaluator`), and otherwise runs
    an implementation of the same published algorithm in
    `cosmos_evaluator/hallucination.py`. Every result records which engine ran.
    Upstream's algorithm — dynamic-mask differencing, distance-transform tolerance,
    and the resulting hallucinated-pixel ratio — is described in that module's
    docstring, and the two engines agree to ~1e-3 on the same clip pair.

  - Attribute verification check (`checks/attribute_verification`). NPA reuses
    upstream's system prompts, per-variable user prompt, guided-JSON response
    schema, and answer parsing verbatim in
    `cosmos_evaluator/attribute_verification.py`. Upstream drives both the
    question-generation LLM and the answering VLM through a configurable
    OpenAI-compatible endpoint; NPA configures Nebius Token Factory instead of
    build.nvidia.com.

Upstream resolves its bundled `cosmos_evaluator.yaml` through Bazel runfiles.
NPA aliases the published `bazel-runfiles` wheel under the Bazel module path so
the checkers import from a plain source checkout; see
`cosmos_evaluator/upstream.py`.

## Cosmos Curator

  https://github.com/nvidia-cosmos/cosmos-curate                (Apache-2.0)
  https://github.com/nvidia-cosmos/cosmos-xenna                 (Apache-2.0)

Wrapped by `npa/src/npa/workbench/cosmos_curate/` and exposed as
`npa workbench cosmos-curate`. Upstream's curation pipelines ship inside its own
pixi-managed container and publish no wheel, so NPA bakes a pinned source checkout
into the `npa-cosmos-curate` image and drives upstream's real stage classes
directly — no Ray scheduler, no GPU:

  VideoDownloader -> FixedStrideExtractorStage -> ClipTranscodingStage
  -> MotionVectorDecodeStage -> MotionFilterStage -> ClipWriterStage

The curation work and the output layout (`clips/`, `metas/v0/`,
`processed_videos/`) are upstream's own; NPA only stages artifacts in and out and
summarizes the result. `split_pipeline_argv` builds upstream's documented
`video-pipeline split` command for operators who run the full curator container
with its GPU stages.

